@using Khangri.UI.Models
@model HomeViewModel

@section styles{
  <style> 
    .text-justify{
        text-align: justify;
    }
  </style>
} 

<div class="inner-banner-section">
    <img src="~/assets/images/bg/inner-banner-vctr.png" class="inner-banner-vector" alt="image">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-xl-8 col-md-10 col-sm-12">
          <div class="breadcrumb-area">
            <span> “Where Every Step is a Story, and Every Peak a Promise.” </span>
            <span>32 Years of Guiding Himalayan Dreams </span>
            <h2>KHANGRI TOURS, TREKS & EXPEDITIONS</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="blog-details-section pt-120 pb-120">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-10">
              <div class="blog-details-single text-justify">
                    <h3 class="blog-details-subtitle">About Us</h3>


                    <p>Founded in 1994, Khangri Tours, Treks & Expeditions has been guiding adventurers, explorers, and dreamers through the magnificent landscapes of Sikkim and the Eastern Himalayas for over three decades.</p>
                  
                    <p>With more than 31 years of experience, we take pride in being one of Sikkim’s most trusted and time-honored adventure travel companies — a name synonymous with authentic Himalayan exploration, safety, and sustainability.</p>

                    <p>Our journey began with a simple vision: to share the untouched beauty of Sikkim with the world, while empowering local communities and preserving our fragile mountain ecosystem. Today, that same spirit continues to guide every trek we organize and every traveler we host. The company is well established organization with many years of experience in conducting tours, treks and expeditions in Sikkim, Ladakh, all India, Nepal ,Tibet and Bhutan.</p>

                    <p>The company registered and recognized as Grade “A” by Government of Sikkim and also awarded as Best international tour operator (Inbound) 2011 & 2013, Sikkim Awards for best tour operator 2022 , Sikkim tourism Best Grade “A” travel agency 2025 . the company has also served as high altitude logistic support for Kailash Mansarovar Yatra 2015 & 2016 Sikkim Chapter.</p>





                    <h3 class="blog-details-subtitle">Our Services</h3>

                    <p>Trekking & Hiking: From gentle village walks to challenging high-altitude expeditions, discover Sikkim’s most breathtaking trails — Dzongri, Goecha La, Singalila Ridge, Green Lake, and more.</p>
                    
                    <p>Peak Expeditions: Conquer the mighty Himalayan summits with experienced mountaineering guides and expert logistical support.</p>
                    
                    <p>Cultural & Nature Tours: Experience the soul of Sikkim through its monasteries, festivals, traditional homestays, and pristine landscapes.</p>
                    
                    <p>Customized Adventure Packages: Tailor-made itineraries for individuals, families, students, and corporate groups.</p>
                    
                    <p>Eco & Responsible Travel: We are committed to Leave-No-Trace principles, local employment, and environmental stewardship.</p>




                    <h3 class="blog-details-subtitle">A Team Built on Trust and Expertise</h3>

                    <p>Our management brings together professionals from diverse backgrounds — tourism management, outdoor leadership, logistics, and hospitality — united by one goal: to deliver exceptional Himalayan adventures.</p>

                    <p>They work hand in hand with local guides, porters, cooks, and support staff, creating a family-like environment where teamwork and respect are paramount. This harmony is what allows us to deliver smooth, safe, and enriching journeys, even in the most remote corners of the Himalayas.</p>




                    <h3 class="blog-details-subtitle">COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT.</h3>

                    <p>Interestingly, since its inception, Khangri Tour Trek and Exped. has been incessantly facilitating and advocating for community development activities. Towards promoting quality responsible tourism, making a significant contribution to Sikkim tourist industry, the Managing Director of Khangri Tours, Treks & Expedition Mr. Tshering Dorjee Lachungpa has been facilitating community development activities covering the underprivileged and needy segments of Sikkim. The company works with the slogan of 'Community Development through Tourism'. The company also encourages its clients who besides trekking and climbing the Himalayas are apprised in contributing towards the development through meaningful positive contribution for the sustainable development of Sikkim especially in rural areas.</p>

              </div>

              <div class="white_content text-center">
                <div class="white-wrapper">
                  <h2>Regions we can take you</h2>
                  <hr class="h2_under">
                  <p><strong>The Himalayan Range</strong></p>
                  <p>Himalaya, meaning “ snow abode” is an uninterrupted range of mountains and peaks that has long fascinated and
                    challenged adventurers. While mountaineers look at it as an ultimate challenge, aspiring trekkers have it on their
                    bucket list. Extending from West to the East in the form of a 2,500 km curve, people come to the Himalaya for many
                    reasons - &nbsp;to seek knowledge, solitude and enlightenment, adventure and challenge.</p>
                  <p>&nbsp;</p>
                  <img src="~/assets/images/custom/map.png" class="img-fluid" alt="image">
                  <p>&nbsp;</p>
                </div>

                <div class="white_content text-center">
                  <div class="white-wrapper ">
                        <h2>Food &amp; Equipment</h2>
                        <hr class="h2_under">
                        <p>Our chefs and kitchen staff routinely produce a mouth-watering spread of tasty, hygienically cooked dishes at every meal. While trekking, a nutritious and tasty packed lunch is provided. We offer Local, Chinese and Continental cuisines and use locally purchased produce. Our meals are carefully designed to be balanced, nutritious and tasty. The emphasis is on a high carbohydrate and largely vegetarian diet, which we have found is more easily digested in the mountains, especially at higher altitudes. We accommodate a wide variety of dietary preferences and have even served gluten free food on occasion. Meal helpings are generous and the drinks and snacks are always plentiful. We provide you with ample safe drinking water throughout a trip – the water is collected from known clean sources and is then boiled, cooled and a dash of iodine added at times as an precautionary measures.</p>
                        <p>&nbsp;</p>
                        <p>We use the highest standard of equipment on all our trips. On our climbing trips we use only UIAA / CE tested climbing equipment. All our equipment undergoes regular preventive maintenance. On treks we offer spacious three-men dome tents on twin- sharing basis so that you have enough personal space along with your equipment. You will be provided with foam mattresses inside the tents to sleep on. All trekking trips include toilet tents (dry pit), spacious kitchen tent and a dining tent with tables and camp stools. On all the trips going to altitudes above 5000m we carry a PAC (Portable Altitude Chamber) and Pulse Oximeters. An exhaustive first aid kit is always carried by the trip leader. With large groups the front and the rear are always covered by our team members equipped with Walkie-Talkie radios.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

              </div>
          </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>            